 (no add/commit/stash/checkout/switch/reset/pull/push; no `jj commit/new/describe/squash/rebase/abandon/bookmark/undo`). Read-only git (log, show, diff, status, rev-parse, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-list, merge-base) is fine. The L1 commits; you do not.\n- Any fixture repo you create must be `D=$(mktemp -d)` + `git -C \"$D\" init -q`, every later git call must name `-C \"$D\"`, and you must check `git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show-toplevel` equals `$D` before the first commit. Never commit with a throwaway identity anywhere else.\n- Scratch: your work dir, clones and fixtures live under $HYAKU_SCRATCH/revenger-r91/<your seat name>/ (HYAKU_SCRATCH defaults to /fast/scratch/hyaku). mkdir -p it, pass it explicitly, never rely on an inherited TMPDIR, and delete it before you yield (`trap 'rm -rf -- \"$S\"' EXIT`). /tmp only for files under 50 MB. Anything a report must cite lands in the lane tree or the wave dir, never /tmp.\n- Your `Report:` trailer path is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/<that path>.\n- You are a leaf: spawn no subagents, run no swarm. Read-only unless your task says to write.\n- Tooling authorization (operator, 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help the task; first read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md (official channels only, never pipe an unverified remote script into a shell; record tool/version/channel/reason in your report). pacman is PAUSED host-wide (orchestrator ruling 2026-10-20): install via `uv tool`/`npx`/an official binary into ~/.local/bin, or install nothing; never `pacman -S`, `-Sy`, `-Syu`, `-U`, `-R`.\n- Honesty: an unrun check has not passed. Report a defect rather than hiding it; a claim you cannot support is reported as unsupported. The frozen files (reports/round-91/claims.md, sm6_battery_v3.py, mutants.py, c1_counter.py, cap_probe.py) are not yours to edit — report a defect instead.\n",
